tyle=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T17:25:18-08:00","id":1499175,"title":"","content":"The Abandoned Meat Factory has definitely got my interest piqued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T17:26:19-08:00","id":1499176,"title":"","content":"All of them.<br /> So many interesting concepts here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27115-glorious-end","name":"Glorious End","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T19:46:26-08:00","id":1499185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499112-entities-from-my-mage-chronicles?p=1499160#post1499160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Sees a reference to the Epic of Gilgamesh</i> I would like to add Tim to the list please, Salakhel as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/Sqr6JCb.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Utnapishtim, Transportation And Combat Droid</b></a><br /> <br /> Built by Doctor Krieger with assistance from several supernaturals with an affinity for machinery, Tim's hardware and software were adapted from the &quot;corpse&quot; of a Rank 3 Psychopomp-Angel sent by the God-Machine to sabotage the ongoing summoning ritual inside the artificial Dead Dominion of Scarab. With a combination of Ephemeral Enchantment, Platonic Form and a lucky combat roll, Doctor Krieger manages to conjure a missile launcher that deals Aggravated Damage to the Angel and forces it to crash-land.<br /> <br /> Via extensive and invasive analysis of the Angel's &quot;corpse&quot;, Doctor Krieger discovers how to haphazardly convert it into a 3 dots Aetheric Generator, something that was considered impossible by most up until then, but Doctor Krieger did not consider writing blueprints to explain how he did it. This Generator is designed to resemble an upside-down crucifixion of the Angel as a violent mockery of the pointless and parasitic &quot;designs&quot; of the God-Machine, and is used to supply Doctor Krieger's assistants with Aether for their shared projects, and to fuel Tim.<br /> <br /> Doctor Krieger rolled for an Act of Hubris due to his reckless idea of using explosives of extreme power inside the cave-like structures of the Underworld and risking an anomalous cave-in, but succeeded on that roll by the skin of his teeth. Tim looks like a combination of a Destroyer Droid from Star Wars and Robotnik's Egg Carrier from Sonic The Hedgehog, and has the voice of a Cyberman from Doctor Who if given human-like emotional inflections.<br /> <br /> Tim usually reserves his anger for combating the enemies of scientific progress, and displays a profound satisfaction when outmaneuvering and exterminating them. Tim is a medium-strength AI, that is, he can make a considerable degree of independent choices, but cannot significantly change as a result of thinking about said choices (i.e. he does not track Experiences and would require Doctor Krieger's help to change, and even then his traits can only be swapped around in ways that maintain his Potency of 7).<br /> <br /> Quote: &quot;IT IS TIME TO DISCOVER AND CLAIM THE LANDS WHERE ANGELS FEAR TO GO!&quot;<br /> <br /> Virtue: Courageous<br /> Vice: Confrontational<br /> Aspirations: Explore the cosmos and its mysteries, assist with scientific researches and experiments, exterminate the enemies of the Pentacle<br /> <br /> Mental Attributes: Intelligence 6, Wits 8, Resolve 4<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 4, Dexterity 8, Stamina 6<br /> Social Attributes: Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 8<br /> <br /> Skills: Crafts (Mechanical Repairs) 5, Occult (God-Machine) 5, Science (High Energy Physics) 5, Drive (High Risk Maneuvers) 5, Firearms (Lasers) 5, Survival (Navigation) 5<br /> <br /> Merits: Common Sense 3, Eidetic Memory 2, Crack Rider 3, Double-Jointed 2, Stunt Driver 4, Firefight 3, Marksmanship 4<br /> <br /> Aether: 35<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Defense: 13 (Calculated With Drive)<br /> Initiative: 16<br /> Speed: Same As A Motorcycle [ChroD Core Page 98]<br /> Health: 15 (Size 9)<br /> Potency: 7<br /> <br /> Ban 1: Must Leave Behind Scientific Symbols When Exploring And Researching<br /> Ban 2: Suffers From The Lost And Amnesia Conditions If Exposed To Very Powerful Magnetic Fields<br /> Bane: A Specific Type Of God-Machine Cryptid Mutated From Woodworms<br /> <br /> Dread Powers: Abruption Jets (Propulsion), Aura Sight (Technology), Directed Energy Weapon (Technology), Nanobot Composition (Process), Rip The Gates (Exploit), Right Tools Right Job (Embed), Synthesis (Embed), Unbreakable, Wings (Propulsion)<br /> <br /> Other Traits: Price Of Power X 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-09-2022, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T21:22:18-08:00","id":1499191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499112-entities-from-my-mage-chronicles?p=1499120#post1499120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vote Jar Friend and/or Shield Maiden.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/glBXKDG.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vitreous Swimmer AKA Happy Jar Friend (Cnidarian-Spirit)</b></a><br /> <br /> The Familiar of Cousteau, a Thyrsus Mystagogue who specializes in genetic-engineering, shamanism and oceanography. Cousteau keeps Vitreous Swimmer inside a custom test tube that looks like a perfume bottle, or rather, that's where he keeps the genetically-engineered pseudo-cnidarian that is the Fetter for the actual Familiar. At one point, this Fetter was transferred to a drone to facilitate communication and manipulation of objects, along with the inclusion of various combat features.<br /> <br /> Quotes:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Jar Friend pokes Umbra in the shoulder with a screwdriver, seemingly taking a childlike joy in the metallic clink noise the poking makes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Materials? Money? Negotiations, steal, violence?&quot; The Jar Friend continues making gestures. &quot;Which Mages? Give what?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Thirsty, need water. Mages need water, Mages living beings. Violence, deny water? Negotiations, Mystery in water?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Thank you, Hypatia,&quot; The Jar Friend takes the water, opens a compartment of its robotic vessel, and pours the water into its gelatinous form.<br /> <br /> &quot;Negotiations, difficult. Mages dangerous, Mages weird. Violence, drowning? Maybe.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Water, origin of all life. Mages, study living creatures? Give water-creature Mystery to Mage, get payment. Use payment for different, metal-worker Mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Cousteau complain. Water-creature must be safe, no violence.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Jar Friend whirs and clicks in an offended manner, akin to huffing and puffing. &quot;Not me! The other water-creature, the octopus! I am jellyfish-born!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Jar Friend stares for several seconds at the printer paper, scratching its metal head in confusion. &quot;I do not understand this. Swimming counts?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Swim through water with sharks!&quot; The Jar Friend says, as if it just discovered the cure for cancer.<br /> <br /> The Jar Friend looks at the Mages and floats around pensively. &quot;Bring outside Mage to solve three problems? Astral knowledge for friend of metal-worker? Dilute and mix efforts, like salt in water.&quot; </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rank: 2<br /> Attributes: Power 4, Finesse 6, Resistance 4<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Essence: 15<br /> Initiative: 10<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Speed: 15 (Species Factor 5)<br /> Size: 2<br /> Corpus: 6<br /> Influences: Water 2<br /> Ban: Cannot use Numina or Influences while exposed to extreme dryness or pollution<br /> Bane 1: Natural Soil<br /> Bane 2: Kitchen Salt<br /> Manifestation: Twilight Form, Fetter, Image, Unfetter, Materialize<br /> Numina: Telepathy, Metamorphosis, Heal, Regenerate, Ravage<br /> Other Traits: Price Of Power X 1<br /> <br /> Ravage Numen: As per Blast, but it gives a Lethal Damage Bonus up to [Rank] for each 1 Essence spent. This has to contend with the opponent's Defense since it is a melee attack, but the Lethal Damage Bonus lasts for the whole scene as opposed to only one attack. Even without spending any Essence, the entity's melee attacks cause +0L Damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-09-2022, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T21:35:04-08:00","id":1499192,"title":"","content":"I <i>adore</i> it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T23:27:01-08:00","id":1499198,"title":"","content":"Happy Jar Friend is adorable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T02:22:44-08:00","id":1499203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499112-entities-from-my-mage-chronicles?p=1499114#post1499114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Kind of wonder what Shield Maiden and Jack Viper are like.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZivgJ5o.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jack Viper \u2013 Pitying Poisoner</b></a><br /> <br /> Little is known with certainty about this ghost, and he isn't confirming or denying anything if he can help it. Most historians among Sleepers agree that he was born to a mentally ill prostitute in London, sometime during the middle of the 19th century. His mother gave birth to him inside a mental asylum, and his father could not be found, nor could his mother be convinced to give any coherent information about how she became pregnant. Jack Viper's real name is likewise unknown, and most historians speculate that his mother's condition compromised her memory, which led her to give her son various names as if suffering from early dementia.<br /> <br /> The ghost doesn't demonstrate any preferences for how to be addressed, and shows an ambivalent attitude toward his almost mythic name. Despite his background, he managed to lead a normal life by the standards of his society, and demonstrated an abnormally high talent for the medical field, especially toxicology and pharmacology. Records claim he would frequently visit his mother in the asylum, but after one of his visits, his mother displayed a brief capacity to remember everything perfectly and demonstrated a type of happiness and calmness previously considered impossible for her by the asylum's staff. She died shortly afterward, with the alleged cause of death being a mistake committed by one of the nurses when administering her various medications.<br /> <br /> Jack Viper, if he was indeed only one man rather than a conglomeration of hearsay and unreliable sources, supposedly caused his mother's death by giving her an untested medication meant to cure her mental illness so she'd remember who her son was. Legend has it that the accidental death he caused while trying to help his mother ended up serving as the initial motivation for him to seek additional, unwilling test subjects in order to perfect his medication and cure all mental illnesses. However, Jack Viper at one point left too many corpses of important people in his wake, and the policemen of London eventually cornered him in his hideout.<br /> <br /> Most of the policemen either died as a result of exposure to chemical traps, or developed incurable forms of psychosis. Jack Viper committed suicide before being taken to prison by drinking an instantly fatal poison from an assassin's teapot, which became the Anchor of his ghost. Many years later, an Acanthus of the Guardians Of The Veil who goes by the Shadow Name of Nostradamus acquired this Anchor and turned the ghost into his Familiar. The two of them cooperate on solving mysteries and crimes both mundane and supernatural, and although their relationship is strictly professional, it shows hints of ideological friction. Nostradamus intends to use his magic in order to develop ways of accurately predicting and reliably stopping all crimes, ideally in such a way that the culprit is publicly caught in the act. Jack Viper does not explain his motivations for such cooperation, and usually restricts himself to smiling vacantly, offering tea and insisting that there is no need to worry.<br /> <br /> Quote: &quot;They were too beautiful, too captivating, too pure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Virtue: Compassion<br /> Vice: Despair<br /> Rank: 2<br /> Attributes: Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4<br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Essence: 15<br /> Integrity: 4<br /> Initiative: 9<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Speed: 15<br /> Size: 5<br /> Corpus: 9<br /> Influences: Anchor (Assassin's Teapot) 2<br /> Ban: Cannot harm any medical professionals who uphold the Hippocratic Oath<br /> Bane: Antidotes made from the toxins produced by an adder<br /> Manifestation: Twilight Form, Fetter, Image, Materialize, Familiar<br /> Numina: Rapture, Perfect Lie, Hallucination, Poison Bearer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-09-2022, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T05:24:08-08:00","id":1499210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1499112-entities-from-my-mage-chronicles?p=1499203#post1499203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZivgJ5o.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jack Viper \u2013 Pitying Poisoner</b></a><br /> <br /> Little is known with certainty about this ghost, and he isn't confirming or denying anything if he can help it. Most historians among Sleepers agree that he was born to a mentally ill prostitute in London, sometime during the middle of the 19th century. His mother gave birth to him inside a mental asylum, and his father could not be found, nor could his mother be convinced to give any coherent information about how she became pregnant. Jack Viper's real name is likewise unknown, and most historians speculate that his mother's condition compromised her memory, which led her to give her son various names as if suffering from early dementia.<br /> <br /> The ghost doesn't demonstrate any preferences for how to be addressed, and shows an ambivalent attitude toward his almost mythic name. Despite his background, he managed to lead a normal life by the standards of his society, and demonstrated an abnormally high talent for the medical field, especially toxicology and pharmacology. Records claim he would frequently visit his mother in the asylum, but after one of his visits, his mother displayed a brief capacity to remember everything perfectly and demonstrated a type of happiness and calmness previously considered impossible for her by the asylum's staff. She died shortly afterward, with the alleged cause of death being a mistake committed by one of the nurses when administering her various medications.<br /> <br /> Jack Viper, if he was indeed only one man rather than a conglomeration of hearsay and unreliable sources, supposedly caused his mother's death by giving her an untested medication meant to cure her mental illness so she'd remember who her son was. Legend has it that the accidental death he caused while trying to help his mother ended up serving as the initial motivation for him to seek additional, unwilling test subjects in order to perfect his medication and cure all mental illnesses. However, Jack Viper at one point left too many corpses of important people in his wake, and the policemen of London eventually cornered him in his hideout.<br /> <br /> Most of the policemen either died as a result of exposure to chemical traps, or developed incurable forms of psychosis. Jack Viper committed suicide before being taken to prison by drinking an instantly fatal poison from an assassin's teapot, which became the Anchor of his ghost. Many years later, an Acanthus of the Guardians Of The Veil who goes by the Shadow Name of Nostradamus acquired this Anchor and turned the ghost into his Familiar. The two of them cooperate on solving mysteries and crimes both mundane and supernatural, and although their relationship is strictly professional, it shows hints of ideological friction. Nostradamus intends to use his magic in order to develop ways of accurately predicting and reliably stopping all crimes, ideally in such a way that the culprit is publicly caught in the act. Jack Viper does not explain his motivations for such cooperation, and usually restricts himself to smiling vacantly, offering tea and insisting that there is no need to worry.<br /> <br /> Quote: &quot;They were too beautiful, too captivating, too pure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Virtue: Compassion<br /> Vice: Despair<br /> Rank: 2<br /> Attributes: Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4<br /> Willpower: 9<br /> Essence: 15<br /> Integrity: 4<br /> Initiative: 9<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Speed: 15<br /> Size: 5<br /> Corpus: 9<br /> Influences: Anchor (Assassin's Teapot) 2<br /> Ban: Cannot harm any medical professionals who uphold the Hippocratic Oath<br /> Bane: Antidotes made from the toxins produced by an adder<br /> Manifestation: Twilight Form, Fetter, Image, Materialize, Familiar<br /> Numina: Rapture, Perfect Lie, Hallucination, Poison Bearer</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice! Very unique character with a unique MO, fitting Ban and Bane, and neat plot hook given how he's a Familiar. Of course the spy wants the poisoner as his agent - deniable means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T07:37:15-08:00","id":1499217,"title":"","content":"Allllllll the Supernal Entities! Alllllllll of them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T00:14:51-08:00","id":1503738,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda losing the motivation to post on these forums to be honest. But I figured that if this is my last post, might as well share something positive that will cheer people up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/tp22yZD.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Marconi, Machine's Best Friend</b></a><br /> <br /> Virtue: Loyal<br /> Vice: Mischievous<br /> Rank: 2<br /> Attributes: Power 4, Finesse 4, Resistance 6<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Pyros: 15<br /> Initiative: 10<br /> Defense: 4<br /> Speed: 18<br /> Size: 3<br /> Corpus: 9<br /> Armor: 2/2<br /> Influences: Computers 2, Happiness 1<br /> Ban: Must leave behind dog-themed and alchemy-themed digital files on any computer he affects with his Influences, Manifestations or Numina<br /> Bane: Strong Magnets<br /> Manifestation: Materialize, Collapsible, Digitalize<br /> Numina: Aggressive Meme, Blast (Electricity), Occult Sight, Mortal Mask<br /> <br /> Notes: Marconi is considered Materialized by default, instead of existing naturally within the Twilight State. Besides digital technology, Marconi treats Prometheans and any other entity, object or location with Pyros as a source of the Resonance Condition, which he can feed from once per day with the usual roll of Power + Finesse, as if he was a Spirit. He regains Willpower from his Virtue and Vice as if he was a mortal. He can communicate verbally, although his understanding of various concepts is still dog-like. Such communication also triggers Disquiet, using Radioheart's own Azoth as the dice pool. He generates the same type of Disquiet as an Unfleshed.<br /> <br /> Whenever Radioheart regains Pyros, he can reflexively transfer any amount to Marconi, as long as the latter is within Radioheart\u2019s immediate vicinity and perceptible. When using Mortal Mask, Marconi does not assume the form of a mortal, he assumes the form of a normal dog. Without the Mortal Mask, he is obviously a robotic canine, but not overtly supernatural. Marconi does not heal Lethal or Aggravated Damage over time, and instead relies on the Digitalize Manifestation or Repairs [Intelligence + Crafts] with an effective Equipment Bonus equal to his Rank due to the significantly modular and streamlined nature of his supernatural hardware and software.<br /> <br /> The Repairs take 1 hour per -1 on the Repairs roll, and each -1 taken removes 1 Lethal Damage. Healing Aggravated Damage via Repairs requires 1 Pyros for each 1 point of Aggravated Damage. Marconi is not affected by Disquiet from Radioheart, but can be affected by Disquiet from other Prometheans. Marconi has General and Ballistic Armor equal to his Rank for free, but does not go into hibernation like a Spirit does when his Corpus is filled with Aggravated Damage, he is simply destroyed.<br /> <br /> The Digitalize Manifestation requires 1 Pyros and lets him exist as an intangible entity of information that can travel along digital networks. This lasts for hours equal to Successes on his Power + Finesse roll, and during each hour he simply inhabits an active digital device but does nothing except rest, he heals 1 Lethal Damage. During this period, he can be detected via suitable programs and might register as malware, but any mundane attempts to detect or remove him suffer a dice penalty equal to his Successes on his Power + Finesse roll, and supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills against his Resistance + Rank. The Collapsible Manifestation lets Marconi reflexively assume the form of any mundane digital device of up to Size 3 with an Equipment Bonus equal to his Rank, and he can spend Pyros to use his Influence over Computers on himself while in Collapsible Form.<br /> <br /> Quotes:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The two of them enter the Portal and sit down within a private room.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, about my dog. Here he is,&quot; He pulls out a generic cube of grey plastic and puts it on the table. He stares at it for several seconds, growing increasingly frustrated. &quot;Come on, Marconi! This is no time to be mischievous! Or rude for that matter! Greet our new friend like a good boy!&quot;<br /> <br /> He looks at you and chuckles awkwardly. &quot;I swear I am not crazy.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u2014 I can tell you aren't.<br /> <br /> Mind Sight reveals that the cube is indeed a self-aware entity. Space Sight reveals that it is hiding within a spatial folding which uses the cube-form as a entryway into baseline reality. Forces Sight reveals that it possess highly sophisticated electronic components which are not detectable via the naked eye.<br /> <br /> As for Radioheart, Mind Sight reveals much the same info, although his thought-patterns seem disjointed, as if he jumps between wildly different ideas at an accelerated rhythm and has to make effort to keep a steady conversation. Forces Sight reveals that his equivalent of a soul-program is running on alchemical hardware, his blood coursing more like lightning than anything else. Space Sight doesn't reveal much, except for a weird and formless device within another spatial folding that uses his entire Pattern as an entryway into baseline reality.<br /> <br /> \u2014 You, however, seem terribly anxious. What is the issue?<br /> \u2014 You don't need to worry about me, I am not going to hurt you.<br /> <br /> &quot;Marconi is hurt. I can't seem to find what the issue is. Can you try talking to him? He usually isn't like this, so I am worried that his wound is messing with his head.&quot;<br /> He gently moves the cube closer to Umbra.<br /> <br /> \u2014 Alright, give me a moment. \u2014 Umbra gives a look around to see that there aren't any curious sleepers in the room they rented out.<br /> She waves a hand through the space above the cube, as her eyes glow almost crackling electric blue. Words of an ancient, yet so familiar language run from her lips like droplets of water in a rain, and the obstacle pays heed.\u2014 run gnosis engine designate:Umbra SOLD MY SOUL TO A SWEET MELODY evocation /. \u2014 as she peers into the cube.<br /> <br /> The critter within the cube has been exposed to some heavy malware while surfing through a digital medium, which seems to be affecting it analogously to a nasty, delirious fever. How exactly software translates into a physical malady in the critter's case is uncertain. Perhaps it was doing something comparable to Umbra's self-uploading?<br /> <br /> \u2014 Your dog watched too much porn, I think.<br /> \u2014 And got a virus.<br /> \u2014 I can try to flush its system, but its world-state is new to me, so what I can do is, suspend it for the time being, learn more, and then flush it.<br /> \u2014 But I can't say whether it will be suffering during this or not, unless you let me knock it out.<br /> \u2014 Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Radioheart makes an expression of great, great concern. &quot;He is just a dog, though. He wouldn't look for that. Maybe he got lost in the dark web? What in the name of Turing Above was he even doing in there? Bah, no matter. Please knock him out, I would not be able to sleep knowing I let him suffer. We can't seem to get his consent, but it's for his own good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Umbra nods and sings a short, discordant lullaby at the cube, passing her hand above it again.<br /> <br /> The dog enters a deep, sleep-like state.<br /> <br /> Umbra sighs, fishing out a spare USB stick from her bag, and looks at the cube and the stick intently as if it were going to help, lips moving through barely audible glossolalia.<br /> <br /> No outward signs of healing appear for several minutes, until the cube suddenly expands and shifts into a six-legged mechanical canine. He appears like a combination of robots built by Boston Dynamics and a model from a Nintendo 64 game. He looks very confused, but also very happy to see his owner and jumps at him. Radioheart returns the critter's affection with a sigh of relief.<br /> <br /> &quot;Go on, then. Show your gratitude to the new friend!&quot; Instructed Radioheart. Marconi holds out a paw for Umbra to shake.<br /> <br /> Umbra smiles and shakes the paw.<br /> \u2014 You're welcome. <hr /><br /> Radioheart takes out a small and featureless cube of grey plastic, putting it on a table. It immediately expands and shifts into a six-legged and polygonal canine robot. His tail is wagging and his ears are spinning like mini satellites.<br /> <br /> &quot;New friend?&quot; Asks the dog in a computerized and cheerful voice.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, Marconi! New friend! ATTACK!&quot; He shouts.<br /> <br /> The dog playfully bites Krieger's ankle and he feels a brief electric shock. Nothing intense enough to hurt, but it certainly startles him due to how damn fast the dog is with his bite.\u200b<br /> <hr /><br /> After rather intense and focused work, Krieger decides to take a break and switch brain into dispersed mode. For some time, he wanders around his Sanctum, consciously removing work information from his brain. It kinda doesn't work, so he decides to study Marconi in detail to get some now insights into advanced robotics. After getting some more coffee (damn, he really needs to Perfect coffee maker some time), he goes looking for the dog.<br /> <br /> Krieger remembers Radioheart mentioning off-hand that Marconi is a mischievous dog, so it is entirely possible that the robotic friend is hiding in plain sight, ready to pull a prank on Krieger.<br /> But how would such a large and distinctive-looking entity even hide?<br /> <br /> Krieger sips the coffee. It's obvious that this dog have some kind of stealth field. Or chameleonic surface. Or... wait, it kinda was built to be compact, wasn't it? What if?...<br /> Krieger starts looking around for brand new objects he never seen around before.<br /> <br /> Krieger doesn't have to look very long: there is a toaster on the hologram table that the Cabal uses for elaborating strategies. Its visuals contrast very starkly with the futuristic Sanctum, it looks a lot more like something from the 1950s. Krieger is tired to the point that he cannot tell with 100% certainty if this toaster was ever there before, but chances are that Marconi is bad at hiding.<br /> <br /> - Found you! - Krieger pokes at the toaster, wondering, if his tired mind doesn't play tricks on him now.<br /> <br /> The toaster responds with a &quot;ching&quot; noise and two slices of toasted bread. No barking, though. There appears to be something written on them. How? Krieger doesn't remember installing any toasters with graphic design functions...<br /> <br /> One toast has &quot;#1&quot; written on it, and says &quot;look at #2&quot;. The other toast has &quot;#2&quot; written on it, and says &quot;look at #1&quot;.<br /> <br /> It appears that Marconi has a goofy sense of humor. He tries to sneak up on Krieger from behind while he is looking at the so-called brain-frying paradox, but accidentally slips on a puddle of coffee that Krieger forgot to clean up and reveals his position.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh... you caught me. Well, I'll get you next time!&quot;<br /> <br /> - You can talk? You are better than most dogs I know, then. - Krieger sips coffee again. - Do you often succeed at startling people?<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course I can talk! I just don't do it often because it messes with people's heads, but Umbra took care of that. She also cured my fever! She is a very nice, clever and pretty lady, and I like her very much! She's almost as cool as Radioheart, and that's no mean feat! Hey, you got something crunchy around here? I'll startle anyone you want if you give me a nice toy to chew on!&quot;<br /> <br /> - Yeah, people are easily impressed with talking dogs. Do you eat organic food too? Or you eat metal?<br /> <br /> &quot;I can eat anything that doesn't immediately kill me. I could eat rotten meat but not a grenade, for example.&quot;<br /> <br /> - So you are like your friend, then? Did you escaped along with him?<br /> <br /> &quot;I think I am like him, yes. But he found me looking for food in a dumpster. I was scared of him at first because I thought he was a human, but he sang to me to calm me down, and it worked like a charm. We've been best friends since!&quot;<br /> <br /> - Are you scared of humans, then?<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, terribly so! But Radioheart told me that he is doing a thing called a Pilgrimage. Some sort of spiritual journey to become a human. He says that it is possible I can go on my own Pilgrimage, but I don't know if I would turn into a normal dog, or a really smart dog who talks.&quot;<br /> <br /> - Hmm. Losing sentience wouldn't be a great result of such grand journey. Where did he learned about this traveling thing? Do they know anything about what happens with animals like you at the end?<br /> <br /> &quot;He says he gets these visions and dreams sometimes. And no, I don't think he knows. My hunch is that I will only become the best version of myself when he completes his journey. But that's OK! I love him to bits and I'll always be there for him!&quot;<br /> <br /> - Visions and dreams? That's interesting. You want to play hide and seek again?<br /> <br /> &quot;You ask me if I want to play! Do Mages like Mysteries?&quot;<br /> <br /> - Some of them hate them, you know. Broken ones. - Krieger sips the coffee again and puts down the cup. - You want to hide or you want to seek?<br /> <br /> &quot;Let's change things around, you hide! How much time you want to find a spot?&quot;<br /> <br /> - Give me a minute or so. That sounds fair to you?<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure! I'm gonna close my eyes now. Get ready!&quot;<br /> <br /> - And to make things more interesting... Supreme Light-Bending! - with those words, Krieger pictures light bending around him with clever use of metamaterials and makes himself disappear from plain sight. After that, he tries to find a place with a lot of sounds and be very quiet here.<br /> <br /> After a minute passes, Krieger can faintly hear Marconi sniffing and snooping around. The robot dog grows increasingly confused, but no less enthusiastic. When he is running out of ideas, he sits and makes whirring and beeping noises.<br /> <br /> &quot;Think, Marconi, think...&quot; He delves deeper into the Sanctum, and comes back with a water pistol in his third pair of limbs. He is listening intently for any possible noises, firing water here and there. It seems that Marconi is assuming that a layer of water molecules would refract the light in such a way as to give away Krieger's position, which demonstrates that the robot dog has some understanding of physics.<br /> <br /> Now that's a smart dog. Damn, is there any mystical dog shelter? I'd like to adopt one. - thinks Krieger, while trying to figure out how to not get smacked by water pistol. Trying to bend the light again? That's going to be pretty complex... Instead, Krieger pictures a portable gravity generator, able to control the vector. After inserting the gear and turning the device &quot;on&quot; in his mind, Krieger slowly changes the vector, lifting off and drifting to the ceiling. He hopes that Marconi won't go there to look and does have some 2D thinking flaws. He has four legs, after all.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are very good at this! But I won't give up just yet! If you aren't on the ground, then by logical extension you are above me!&quot;<br /> <br /> With internal shrug, Krieger floats up to the middle of the room and starts rotating vector slightly to keep himself in the middle.<br /> <br /> Marconi looks around inside drawers and cabinets, until he finds a rubber ball. &quot;Ah-ha! Prepare to meet your doom, Krieger!&quot; He tosses the rubber ball with a surprising amount of force, which starts bouncing around wildly.<br /> <br /> Now that's just nasty! - Krieger thinks. He is trying to put his intuition and knowledge of physics to trying to guess the trajectory of the ball and keep himself away from it with gravity control.<br /> <br /> Krieger easily dodges the rubber ball. Marconi watches it slowly lose momentum, completely enraptured by the crazy trajectories. After some time, he looks around and does a shrug-like gesture.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I can't explode our home just to find you! I surrender, you win!&quot;<br /> <br /> - You were close. - Krieger drops the invisibility and slowly goes back to the ground before dismissing gravity control. - I kinda expected you to find me by smell of coffee, to be honest.<br /> <br /> &quot;...that smell was you? I thought it was one of those things which tried to eat Radioheart once,&quot; Said Marconi semi-jokingly.<br /> <br /> - Which things? And yes, my smells are coffee, dust, metal and those weird living things you can find in roaches and eat. Remember that if you'll ever need to find me by smell! - says Krieger also semi-jokingly.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know what that thing was called, where it came from, or anything like that. But it looked like a statue at first.&quot;<br /> <br /> - Huh. Now that's scary stuff. I once made living metal statue going haywire. Tried to kill me before I melted it down in a hurry. - Krieger winces. - Now it's your turn to hide. How much time do you need?<br /> <br /> &quot;A minute. Go ahead and start counting!&quot;<br /> <br /> Krieger starts counting to 60 seconds.<br /> <br /> After the countdown is over, Krieger looks through the Sanctum for any object which sticks out from the rest. He is not finding anything with the naked eye alone, but Marconi did not give any impression of expecting Krieger to not use magic.<br /> <br /> - Now, now, how can I find one smart little dog... Analyze Frequencies! - Krieger declares in High Speech, extending his hearing range into ultra- and infrasound frequencies. He tries to find some unusual sounds which could be made by Marconi's inner mechanisms.<br /> <br /> Krieger hears some unusual sounds coming from the cafeteria section, little beeping and whirring noises. As Krieger focuses on the source, he has the impression it is coming from somewhere above him.<br /> <br /> Krieger goes to cafeteria section and grabs another cup of coffee, making impression of not having a clue where to look, while actually listening closely to sounds above. Is it Marconi?<br /> <br /> Krieger hears a very faint canine equivalent of laughter coming from above him. That and the familiar noise of helices turning.<br /> <br /> Krieger looks upward and points at source of the laughter.<br /> <br /> - I caaaaaaaan heeeeeeeeaaaaaar youuuuuuuu!<br /> <br /> Marconi has adopted the form of a semi-transparent and toy-like drone, the sort that children play with via remote control.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, drat. I let my excitement get the best of me yet again!&quot; He slowly descends to the floor and turns into a dog again. &quot;You were a good sport about this, thank you very much.&quot;<br /> <br /> - And so were you. Laughing is the part that got you. I didn't get the chance to study you in detail, will you allow me to do so?<br /> <br /> &quot;But of course. As long as I remain in one piece by the end of it. You won't be using me for any crazy and highly dubious experiments, will you?&quot;<br /> <br /> - Not without your consent, no. And I won't even use a plasma torch! Just look at you weirdly and drool a bit.<br /> <br /> &quot;Drool? That's weird, I thought I was the dog in this situation. You might wanna ask Reptilian to fix your salivation glands. Anyway, go ahead and scan me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Krieger begins to Scrutinize him with Focused Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Krieger sees that Marconi is not just an alchemical construct; he is a genuine living being whose inner workings simply happen to obey principles of metal, silica and plastic. He possess a potential for evolution and adaptation, albeit interlinked with the spiritual development of Radioheart. It is safe to assume that if Radioheart were to die or become irrevocably lost, Marconi would stagnate until he found another Promethean to bond with. It is almost as if whatever entity/force/system which is responsible for animating Prometheans has created Marconi specifically to be an incentive for Radioheart to become human. If this is true, other such sidekicks and pets might exist out there, which implies some degree of intent or purpose behind the Divine Fire. And if that phenomenon is capable of communication with humans in a decipherable manner, a Mage like Krieger might stand to learn unprecedented secrets about artificial intelligence if he can manage to contact an avatar of the Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> -Hmm. You like Radioheart, do you?<br /> <br /> &quot;Absolutely, without a shadow of doubt! He is my very best friend! When I was sick, he would do his best to fix me, and would cry into the little hours of the morning for not finding a cure. Even though he has only a backpack of possessions, he is always looking for things to give to me as toys. He taught me all he knows about humans and is an inspiration to me!&quot;<br /> <br /> - Well, stick to him. He needs you more than you or he think. You are something of a catalyst for him to grow, understand? You mentioned he has visions?<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, yes. But you are better served asking him about those visions, don't you agree?&quot;<br /> <br /> - Yes, but I am not asking about content of visions. How does he looks like when he has them? Did you noticed something strange about him?<br /> <br /> &quot;There is not much of a pattern, I am afraid. Sometimes he looks utterly terrified, other times it looks like he is completely at peace with himself and the universe. But these visions never seem to lead him astray, even if they cause him a lot of pain in some way or another.&quot;<br /> <br /> - Yeah, okay. - Krieger rubs his chin. - You are a good dog. Keep it this way, will you?<br /> <br /> &quot;Affirmative! Like that one movie says, all dogs go to heaven. But it would be terribly lonely up there without Radioheart.&quot;<br /> <br /> - Nah, I am pretty sure you'll end up wherever he goes. - Krieger stands up. - Thank you. I'd wish I had a dog like you. Radioheart is terribly lucky in his own way.<br /> <br /> After this, Krieger returns to his work on AI prototype.\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T04:34:24-08:00","id":1503746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quot